      ],
      "description": "The two `Library` strippers, moved down from the WHO build's \"DAK Postprocessing\" phase because neither is DAK-shaped -- any IG depending on `hl7.fhir.uv.cql` produces oversized `Library` resources. Declared here rather than only described in a skill: a layer boundary that exists in prose is one no consumer can act on, and these were described as belonging here for a whole round while being declared nowhere.",
      "readmePath": "tools/README.md",
